7. THE TIMING on printed figures and the drafted rows: the restart, the recovery interval, the rate
   THE DECISION (DRAFTED, W143-D5): a controller asserts its restart vote on a peer when it has captured no edge on either of that
     peer's TXDs (its own TIM3 captures) and received no state frame of it on either fabric for 2.0 s, at most once in 10 s per peer,
     and holds it 2.0 s; it needs no fabric and never votes on a message received over one. A running controller is never that
     silent: with both fabrics stopped by FW-B21 it still probes each once a second (1.1 s cycle, l9t5_canq.py CFG), and a booting
     controller rejoins within 0.800 s (l9t5_canq.out section 8: boot, ASSUMPTION, MON 2 windows, its slot), both under 2.0 s
   the two peers' votes start within 1.081 ms of each other (each evaluates within 1 ms, DRAFTED; two crystals' +-20 ppm over the
     decision; the read-back copy of a TXD edge 1012 ns): they see the same last edge through the same buffers
   THE RESTART: the FET's gate passes 2.5 V within 1.208 s of the second vote (the RC's largest time constant 0.475 s: 100k 1% and 1M 1% at
     their 1 %, 4.7uF +10 %, ASSUMPTION), so EN is held under VIL for at least 0.791 s of the 2.0 s hold, against the 3 ms the
     limiter's turn-off takes at most (SLVS841F 7.5, PRINTED) and the 0.5 s this route requires (DRAFTED): "the device enable is toggled"
   THE RETURN: the votes released, the FET's gate falls under its least threshold within 0.799 s; EN rises through 10k 1%; the limiter turns
     on within 3 ms (SLVS841F 7.5, PRINTED, CL 1 uF, RL 100 Ohm), the TPS73733 starts in 431 us (SBVS067W 5.6, new silicon: TYP, no maximum
     printed), and the controller boots, listens 2 windows in bus monitoring mode and sends in its slot within 0.800 s (W139's bound)
   THE RECOVERY INTERVAL of a latched supervisor, its cause gone: 2.0 s (decision) + 1 ms + 2.0 s (hold) + 0.799 s (release) +
     3 ms + 431 us (TYPICAL) + 0.800 s = 5.603 s (MODEL on PRINTED, DRAFTED and the boot ASSUMPTION); before this round: NONE,
     an operator's power cycle
   a persistent cause: the limiter latches again after its 5 to 10 ms deglitch (PRINTED) and the peers try again 10 s after their
     last vote: at most 24.2 mJ an attempt (record l4reg's MODEL at the limiter's maximum), 2.42 mW on average; the other two keep the quorum throughout (IOHA row 3)
   with two supervisors latched the third cannot restart either (2 of 2 needs both peers): row 4's outcome until RAIL_EN is cycled;
     with all three latched (row 8 with W138's limiter, R8b) only RAIL_EN returns them, as W139 found
   a supervisor held off on the bench (IOHA A4 and A6, J_IOCOFF fitted) is restarted every 10 s by its peers: harmless, its LDO's EN
     stays held (finding W143-F9)
   timing holds: yes

8. THE ROUTE'S OWN FAULTS (per supervisor) and the route's in-service test
   THE TEST rides on the restated self-test (l9t5_canmb.out section 7): in the windows of the fabric A target X, P_EN in its P1 and P2
     windows pulses one peer's restart vote on X from 68 to 72 ms of that peer's window, V_EN in its V window both peers', and X reads
     its restart gate's output from 66 to 74 ms of its own (the windows aligned within 1.0 ms, so each pulse lies inside the read span
     and V_EN's two pulses overlap 2 ms or more): P_EN reads low, V_EN high, and a fault is declared on the second consecutive failure;
     the verdicts travel on either fabric, so the route's test keeps its interval, 2.60 s, with one fabric down; one cycle 1.2000 s
   element                                          fault                       effect                                                 found by                              bound
   a restart vote output, its line or its gate input stuck low or open           the route cannot restart the target                    V_EN fails                            within 2.60 s
   a restart vote output, its line or its gate input stuck high                  one peer alone could switch the target off (1 of 1)    the other peer's P_EN fails           within 2.60 s
   a peer's restart decision (firmware)             votes without cause         as a vote stuck high: alone it switches nothing        the other peer's P_EN fails           within 2.60 s
   a peer's restart decision (firmware)             dead                        the route cannot restart the target                    NOT in service: RESIDUAL (recovery)   none
   a restart vote pull-down (10 kOhm)               short                       as its vote stuck low                                  V_EN fails                            within 2.60 s
   a restart vote pull-down (10 kOhm)               open                        floats only while its voter is in reset or dark        NOT in service: RESIDUAL              none
   the restart gate                                 output stuck low            the route cannot restart the target                    V_EN fails                            within 2.60 s
   the restart gate                                 output stuck high           the FET turns on: the target switched off (IOHA row 3) its frames absent                     within 1.311 s
   the gate's 100 Ohm feed                          open                        the gate unpowered: no restart                         V_EN fails                            within 2.60 s
   the gate's 100 Ohm feed                          short                       none until its 100 nF also shorts (then the next rail) NOT in service: RESIDUAL              none
   the gate's 100 nF                                short                       the gate unpowered (next rail loaded, inside its limit) V_EN fails                            within 2.60 s
   the RC's 100 kOhm                                open                        the FET never turns on: no restart                     NOT in service: RESIDUAL (recovery)   none
   the RC's 100 kOhm                                short                       no delay: a V_EN pulse reaches the FET                 V_EN: the target resets, one restart  within 2.60 s, the target back within 0.803 s
   the RC's 4.7 uF                                  open                        no delay (the FET's own Ciss, TYPICAL only)            V_EN: the target resets, one restart  within 2.60 s, the target back within 0.803 s
   the RC's 4.7 uF                                  short                       the FET never turns on: no restart                     NOT in service: RESIDUAL (recovery)   none
   the FET's 1 MOhm                                 short                       the FET never turns on: no restart                     NOT in service: RESIDUAL (recovery)   none
   the FET's 1 MOhm                                 open                        its gate rests on leakage only while the gate is unpowered NOT in service: RESIDUAL              none
   the AO3400A                                      drain-source short          EN held low: the target switched off (IOHA row 3)      its frames absent                     within 1.311 s
   the AO3400A                                      open, or gate-source short  no restart                                             NOT in service: RESIDUAL (recovery)   none
   the 470 Ohm                                      open                        no restart                                             NOT in service: RESIDUAL (recovery)   none
   the 470 Ohm                                      short                       none (it bounds a shorted pull-up's current)           NOT in service: RESIDUAL              none
   the EN pull-up (10 kOhm)                         open                        EN floats: the limiter may switch off (IOHA row 3)     its frames absent                     within 1.311 s
   the EN pull-up (10 kOhm)                         short                       EN cannot be pulled low: no restart                    NOT in service: RESIDUAL (recovery)   none
   the read-back's 10 kOhm                          open                        the target cannot see its gate: V_EN reads low         V_EN fails (a route fault flagged)    within 2.60 s
   the read-back's 10 kOhm                          short                       a faulty target reaches the gate's output directly     NOT in service: RESIDUAL              none
   the target's read-back input                     stuck                       P_EN or V_EN reads wrong                               that phase fails                      within 2.60 s
   12 residuals, 7 of them of the recovery only (a latched supervisor then waits for RAIL_EN, the state before this round); none
     switches a healthy supervisor off or lets one peer do so alone; the faults that switch a supervisor off are single faults of its
     own power path, IOHA row 3, found at once; the one fault that leaves a 1-of-1 route (a vote stuck high, or a decision that votes
     without cause) is found within 2.60 s by the other peer's P_EN, without switching anything off
   NOT TAKEN (W143-D7): a start-up restart of each supervisor by its peers, which would bound the recovery residuals by the kit's power
     cycle at the cost of switching every healthy supervisor off once per start; the residuals stay named and are injected on the
     first article (section 10, the supplier's tasks)

