     (M1c's GPIO jammer on both fabrics) reads "quorum lost" on both schedules against M1c's required "a node out and contained", which
     the restated stop gives ("a node out and contained"): the single-window stop FAILS the jammer row (the test re-runs it, test_l4canen.py)
   consistent with the corrected drafts: the self-test never silences a state frame (its hold lies outside every slot,
     l9t5_canmb.out section 7), so no test phase can starve a fabric of valid frames toward the stop; a fabric the stop holds is
     probed once a second, so its controller's TXDs move within 1.1 s, under the restart decision's 2.0 s: the stop never invites a
     restart; and the stopped fabric's self-test phases wait for it while the other fabric's run: yes
